#: codec/1/272/0x110ab0/25
msgid ""
"Fishing with Chico, cooking with Amanda and\n"
"Cecile, playing soccer,\n"
msgstr ""
"和奇科钓鱼，和阿曼达、\n"
"塞西尔做饭，踢足球，\n"

#: codec/1/272/0x110ab0/26
msgid ""
"having visitors when I caught a cold...\n"
msgstr ""
"感冒时有人来探望我……\n"

#: codec/1/272/0x110ab0/27
msgid ""
"When I stop and think about it, my time here has\n"
"been the most peaceful of my life.\n"
msgstr ""
"静下心想想，在这里的日子\n"
"是我一生中最平静的时光。\n"

#: codec/1/272/0x110ab0/28
msgid ""
"But that is about to end.\n"
msgstr ""
"但这一切就要结束了。\n"

#: codec/1/272/0x110ab0/29
msgid ""
"I cannot imagine he'll be willing to negotiate.\n"
msgstr ""
"我不认为他愿意谈判。\n"

#: codec/1/272/0x110ab0/30
msgid ""
"It seems I am to fight the legendary Big Boss.\n"
msgstr ""
"看来我要与传说中的BIG BOSS一战。\n"

#: codec/1/272/0x110ab0/31
msgid ""
"I don't know if I'll be able to beat him,\n"
msgstr ""
"我不知道能否战胜他，\n"

#: codec/1/272/0x110ab0/32
msgid ""
"but if I have to choose between death and defying\n"
"Cipher, I will gladly choose death.\n"
msgstr ""
"但若要在死亡与背叛CIPHER\n"
"之间选择，我宁愿去死。\n"

#: codec/1/272/0x110ab0/33
msgid ""
"The thought of dying does not scare me.\n"
msgstr ""
"想到死，我并不害怕。\n"

#: codec/1/272/0x110ab0/34
msgid ""
"But if I disobey my orders, the fear and despair\n"
"awaiting me will be far worse than anything I can\n"
"imagine.\n"
msgstr ""
"可若违抗命令，等着我的\n"
"恐惧与绝望，将远超\n"
"我所能想象的一切。\n"

#: codec/1/272/0x110ab0/35
msgid ""
"It was Cipher who took me in as an orphan - gave\n"
"me food and a place to live.\n"
msgstr ""
"是CIPHER收留了孤儿的我，\n"
"给我食物和住处。\n"

#: codec/1/272/0x110ab0/36
msgid ""
"His orders may have been unreasonable, but I will\n"
"never repay my debt entirely.\n"
msgstr ""
"他的命令或许无理，但这份\n"
"恩情我永远还不清。\n"

#: codec/1/272/0x110ab0/37
msgid ""
"It seems I have no choice. I must fight this man... I\n"
"must fight Snake.\n"
msgstr ""
"看来我别无选择。我必须与\n"
"这个人……与斯内克一战。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/0
msgid ""
"D'you know Miller, Snake's right hand man?\n"
msgstr ""
"你认识Snake的左右手米勒吗？\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/1
msgid ""
"Apparently he's got at least one serious weakness.\n"
msgstr ""
"据说他有个致命的弱点。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/2
msgid ""
"He is an insatiable womanizer.\n"
msgstr ""
"他是个不知餍足的花花公子。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/3
msgid ""
"He does not bother me, most likely because he\n"
"considers teenagers off limits.\n"
msgstr ""
"他不骚扰我，大概是因为\n"
"他把少女排除在外。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/4
msgid ""
"But he has hit on every single one of the few\n"
"female solders here at Mother Base.\n"
msgstr ""
"可母基地里为数不多的女兵，\n"
"他一个都不放过。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/5
msgid ""
"They ought to be telling him where to stick it, but\n"
"end up falling for it so easily.\n"
msgstr ""
"她们本该让他滚蛋，\n"
"却一个个轻易上钩。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/6
msgid ""
"I think some of it stems from the fact that he is\n"
"actually not that bad looking.\n"
msgstr ""
"我想部分原因是\n"
"他其实长得不差。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/7
msgid ""
"Anyway, today that nasty habit got him in trouble.\n"
msgstr ""
"总之，今天这恶习让他惹祸了。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/8
msgid ""
"He and Snake got into one of their rare fights, and\n"
"I was there to see it.\n"
msgstr ""
"他和Snake难得地打了一架，\n"
"我正好在场。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/9
msgid ""
"They burst out of the showers, completely naked,\n"
"trading punches.\n"
msgstr ""
"两人一丝不挂地冲出浴室，\n"
"拳脚相加。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/10
msgid ""
"I am no child - the sight of a naked man doesn't\n"
"make me blush. But this was something else.\n"
msgstr ""
"我不是小孩子——看到裸男\n"
"不会脸红。可这次不一样。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/11
msgid ""
"\"Maybe this'll teach you!\" Snake yelled as he\n"
"slammed his fists into Miller's chest.\n"
msgstr ""
"「这下长记性了吧！」Snake大喊着，\n"
"双拳砸向米勒的胸口。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/12
msgid ""
"I heard later that apparently he'd been two-timing\n"
"someone...\n"
msgstr ""
"后来听说，\n"
"他好像脚踏两条船……\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/13
msgid ""
"and that same someone had gone to Snake with\n"
"her troubles.\n"
msgstr ""
"而那个受害者\n"
"跑去向Snake诉苦。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/14
msgid ""
"As I see it, it is her own fault for letting herself be\n"
"deceived like that.\n"
msgstr ""
"在我看来，\n"
"被人骗成那样是她自己的错。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/15
msgid ""
"If she's too dumb to see though Miller's lies, then\n"
"she got what she deserved.\n"
msgstr ""
"蠢到看不穿米勒的谎言，\n"
"那是她自作自受。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/16
msgid ""
"But this was not the first time it had happened, or\n"
"the second, and Snake read Miller the riot act.\n"
msgstr ""
"可这不是第一次，也不是第二次，\n"
"Snake把米勒狠狠训了一顿。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/17
msgid ""
"Miller argued back, and what began as a shouting\n"
"match turned into a fistfight.\n"
msgstr ""
"米勒顶了几句，\n"
"争吵就变成了互殴。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/18
msgid ""
"\"You son of a bitch!\" Miller yelled as he swung.\n"
msgstr ""
"「你这混蛋！」米勒边骂边挥拳。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/19
msgid ""
"\"Not bad,\" said Snake, smiling. \"But not good\n"
"enough!\" And then he was back on the offensive.\n"
msgstr ""
"「不错，」Snake笑着说，\n"
"「但还不够！」随即又攻了上去。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/20
msgid ""
"They had already been at it pretty hard in the\n"
"showers, and their bodies were covered with\n"
"bruises.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们在淋浴间里已经打得\n"
"很凶，浑身上下\n"
"都是淤青。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/21
msgid ""
"Both of these men had been trained for war, their\n"
"bodies deadly weapons.\n"
msgstr ""
"两人都受过战争训练，\n"
"身体就是致命武器。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/22
msgid ""
"They were each bleeding from a dozen places.\n"
msgstr ""
"两人身上各有十几处在流血。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/23
msgid ""
"All this from a fistfight.\n"
msgstr ""
"而这仅仅是赤手空拳。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/24
msgid ""
"Even so, it was far less gruesome than if they had\n"
"given it their all.\n"
msgstr ""
"即便如此，比起全力以赴，\n"
"已经算不上惨烈。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/25
msgid ""
"It was obvious that one of them would be dead\n"
"were they fighting for real.\n"
msgstr ""
"显而易见，若真拼生死，\n"
"其中一个早就死了。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/26
msgid ""
"Miller took another swing, yelling, \"Try this, then!\"\n"
msgstr ""
"米勒又挥一拳，吼道：“这招如何！”\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/27
msgid ""
"Snake parried, then responded in kind.\n"
msgstr ""
"斯内克格开，随即回敬一拳。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/28
msgid ""
"But I could tell he was not aiming for anything vital.\n"
msgstr ""
"但我看得出来，他没往要害打。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/29
msgid ""
"\"You're one tough bastard, Boss...\" Miller muttered.\n"
msgstr ""
"“你可真硬，BOSS……”米勒嘟囔道。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/30
msgid ""
"A smile crept across his face as he caught his\n"
"breath.\n"
msgstr ""
"他一边喘气，一边\n"
"露出了笑容。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/31
msgid ""
"And then they went right on fighting.\n"
msgstr ""
"然后两人又继续打了起来。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/32
msgid ""
"Blood and sweat flew off their glistening bodies.\n"
msgstr ""
"汗水与鲜血从他们发亮的身体上飞溅。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/33
msgid ""
"It was combat without hatred or hostile intent. I'd\n"
"never seen violence like this before.\n"
msgstr ""
"那是没有恨意与敌意的打斗。\n"
"我从没见过这样的暴力。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/34
msgid ""
"And yet it was more than just a friendly tussle.\n"
"They were utilizing every technique they knew.\n"
msgstr ""
"可又不止是玩闹。\n"
"两人使出了浑身解数。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/35
msgid ""
"It was not a sporting match - they were not\n"
"playing by rules. How could they keep this up?\n"
msgstr ""
"那不是比赛——没有规则可言。\n"
"他们怎能这样打下去？\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/36
msgid ""
"At last, the two men tired themselves out, and the\n"
"bizarre scene came to an end.\n"
msgstr ""
"终于，两人力竭，\n"
"这场闹剧才算收场。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/37
msgid ""
"They looked at each other's battered bodies, and\n"
"then burst out laughing,\n"
msgstr ""
"他们看着彼此伤痕累累的身体，\n"
"随即大笑起来，\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/38
msgid ""
"embracing and congratulating each other on a\n"
"good fight.\n"
msgstr ""
"互相拥抱，称赞这场\n"
"痛快的一架。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/39
msgid ""
"It all seemed so idiotic.\n"
msgstr ""
"这一切都蠢得可笑。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/40
msgid ""
"I still cannot fathom such behavior.\n"
msgstr ""
"我至今无法理解这种行为。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/41
msgid ""
"But somehow I got the sense that for all his\n"
"womanizing,\n"
msgstr ""
"但不知为何我感觉到，别看他\n"
"风流成性，\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/42
msgid ""
"Miller really only trusted one person, and that was\n"
"Snake.\n"
msgstr ""
"米勒真正信任的人只有一个，\n"
"那就是斯内克。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/43
msgid ""
"There was no way I could ever come between the\n"
"two of them.\n"
msgstr ""
"我永远插不进\n"
"他们两人之间。\n"

#: codec/1/273/0x111960/44
msgid ""
"And at that thought I began to feel as if I had lost.\n"
msgstr ""
"想到这里，我开始觉得自己输了。\n"

#: codec/1/274/0x112b00/0
msgid ""
"All of Mother Base is preparing for a festival.\n"
msgstr ""
"整个母基地都在筹备庆典。\n"

#: codec/1/274/0x112b00/1
msgid ""
"Since Snake and his soldiers spend so much time\n"
"fighting,\n"
msgstr ""
"因为Snake和士兵们\n"
"常年征战，\n"

#: codec/1/274/0x112b00/2
msgid ""
"they're setting aside one day a year for peace and\n"
"relaxation.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以每年留出一天\n"
"用来和平与休憩。\n"

#: codec/1/274/0x112b00/3
msgid ""
"I do not know all the details, but apparently that is\n"
"what Snake and Miller decided.\n"
msgstr ""
"细节我不清楚，\n"
"听说是Snake和米勒定的。\n"

#: codec/1/274/0x112b00/4
msgid ""
"The soldiers love the idea, of course.\n"
msgstr ""
"士兵们当然举双手赞成。\n"

#: codec/1/274/0x112b00/5
msgid ""
"There is so little fun to be had here that\n"
"everybody looks forward to events like these.\n"
msgstr ""
"这里实在没什么乐子，\n"
"大家都盼着这种活动。\n"

#: codec/1/274/0x112b00/6
msgid ""
"That is all well and good, but somehow I got roped\n"
"into getting on stage...\n"
msgstr ""
"这倒没什么，\n"
"可我不知怎么被拉上了台……\n"

#: codec/1/274/0x112b00/7
msgid ""
"\"C'mon, we even both have 'peace' in our names,\"\n"
"said Miller.\n"
msgstr ""
"「来嘛，咱俩名字里都有『和平』，」\n"
"米勒说。\n"

#: codec/1/274/0x112b00/8
msgid ""
"\"And Zadornov - that old Russkie's name has\n"
"something to do with peace, too, right?\n"
msgstr ""
"「还有扎多尔诺夫——那俄国佬的名字\n"
"也跟和平有关，对吧？\n"

#: codec/1/274/0x112b00/9
msgid ""
"\"Hey, as long as we're having a day of peace, we\n"
"ought to get an act together - The Three Peace\n"
"Band!\"\n"
msgstr ""
"「既然要办和平日，\n"
"干脆组个乐队——\n"
"和平三人组！」\n"

#: codec/1/274/0x112b00/10
msgid ""
"I thought he was joking.\n"
msgstr ""
"我以为他在开玩笑。\n"

#: codec/1/274/0x112b00/11
msgid ""
"He then proceeded to share his idea without\n"
"bothering to check with me, and now I am slated\n"
"to sing.\n"
msgstr ""
"他不问我的意见就四处宣扬，\n"
"现在我已被安排\n"
"上台演唱。\n"

#: codec/1/274/0x112b00/12
msgid ""
"Apparently, he had heard me on deck one day and\n"
"since then he's wanted to form a band.\n"
msgstr ""
"听说他某天在甲板上听见我唱歌，\n"
"从此就想组乐队。\n"

#: codec/1/274/0x112b00/13
msgid ""
"Everybody's looking forward to it, so there is no\n"
"way for me to back out now.\n"
msgstr ""
"大家都很期待，\n"
"我现在没法推了。\n"

#: codec/1/274/0x112b00/14
msgid ""
"I have never done anything like this, but it does\n"
"feel kind of nice to know that people are looking\n"
"forward to it.\n"
msgstr ""
"我从没做过这种事，\n"
"但知道有人期待，\n"
"心里也有点高兴。\n"

#: codec/1/274/0x112b00/15
msgid ""
"I mean, it cannot be any worse than Miller's singing.\n"
msgstr ""
"我是说，总不会比米勒唱歌更难听吧。\n"

#: codec/1/274/0x112b00/16
msgid ""
"But modifications to ZEKE are already finalized, and\n"
"I must complete my mission.\n"
msgstr ""
"但ZEKE的改装已经定型，\n"
"我必须完成任务。\n"

#: codec/1/274/0x112b00/17
msgid ""
"Betray Cipher now, and I will face a fate far worse\n"
"than death.\n"
msgstr ""
"此刻背叛CIPHER，等着我\n"
"的将比死亡更惨。\n"

#: codec/1/274/0x112b00/18
msgid ""
"Still...\n"
msgstr ""
"可是……\n"

#: codec/1/274/0x112b00/19
msgid ""
"There's no need to put things in motion just yet.\n"
msgstr ""
"还不必现在就动手。\n"

#: codec/1/274/0x112b00/20
msgid ""
"What difference would it make to just wait a little\n"
"while longer?\n"
msgstr ""
"再多等一会儿，\n"
"又能怎样呢？\n"

#: codec/1/274/0x112b00/21
msgid ""
"A whole day of peace...\n"
msgstr ""
"一整天的和平……\n"

#: codec/1/274/0x112b00/22
msgid ""
"The mission can wait until after that, can it not?\n"
msgstr ""
"任务等到那天之后再执行，不行吗？\n"

#: codec/1/274/0x112b00/23
msgid ""
"I know I am only delaying the inevitable.\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道自己只是在拖延。\n"

#: codec/1/274/0x112b00/24
msgid ""
"When the day comes, one of us will have to die -\n"
"Snake or me.\n"
msgstr ""
"到了那天，我们之间\n"
"必须死一个——斯内克，或我。\n"

#: codec/1/274/0x112b00/25
msgid ""
"But still...\n"
msgstr ""
"但还是……\n"

#: codec/1/274/0x112b00/26
msgid ""
"If I could just come up with some way to stall\n"
"Cipher... at least until our day of peace...\n"
msgstr ""
"若能想出办法拖住CIPHER……\n"
"至少拖到那个和平之日……\n"

#: codec/1/274/0x112b00/27
msgid ""
"When did I start having thoughts like this...?\n"
msgstr ""
"我是什么时候开始这样想的……？\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/0
msgid ""
"My cover is blown!\n"
msgstr ""
"我的身份暴露了！\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/1
msgid ""
"They know nothing of Cipher or my true objective,\n"
"but they know I am a spy.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们还不知道Cipher和我的真正目的，\n"
"但已经知道我是间谍。\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/2
msgid ""
"There's no more time left. I must act now.\n"
msgstr ""
"没有时间了。我必须现在行动。\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/3
msgid ""
"I must complete my mission...\n"
msgstr ""
"我必须完成任务……\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/4
msgid ""
"How did it come to this... All I wanted was three\n"
"more days, just three...\n"
msgstr ""
"怎么会走到这一步……\n"
"我只想要三天，只要三天……\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/5
msgid ""
"Miller's already finished writing the song. It's called\n"
"\"Love Deterrent (KOI NO YOKUSHI-RYOKU)\"\n"
msgstr ""
"米勒已经把歌写好了。\n"
"曲名是《恋爱的威慑力》。\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/6
msgid ""
"- it is about a girl who can't express her true\n"
"feelings.\n"
msgstr ""
"——唱的是个无法表达\n"
"真心意的女孩。\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/7
msgid ""
"I have been practicing.\n"
msgstr ""
"我一直在练习。\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/8
msgid ""
"I am no pro, but I was pretty sure I would do a\n"
"decent job.\n"
msgstr ""
"我算不上专业，\n"
"但本来有把握唱得还行。\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/9
msgid ""
"And now this...\n"
msgstr ""
"可现在……\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/10
msgid ""
"Cipher found out that ZEKE was complete.\n"
msgstr ""
"Cipher得知ZEKE已经完工。\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/11
msgid ""
"He must have someone inside Mother Base besides\n"
"me.\n"
msgstr ""
"除了我，母基地里\n"
"一定还有他的人。\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/12
msgid ""
"Spinning his tightly wound web of control, leaving\n"
"no room for individual will - typical.\n"
msgstr ""
"他精心编织控制之网，\n"
"不留半点个人意志——老样子。\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/13
msgid ""
"When they found out ZEKE was complete, I was\n"
"ordered to execute the operation immediately.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们得知ZEKE完工后，\n"
"就命令我立即执行作战。\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/14
msgid ""
"If I was going to enjoy just one day of peace, I had\n"
"to ensure the plan could not move forward.\n"
msgstr ""
"要想享受哪怕一天的和平，\n"
"我就得让计划无法推进。\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/15
msgid ""
"...I tried to sabotage ZEKE.\n"
msgstr ""
"……我试图破坏ZEKE。\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/16
msgid ""
"I thought by damaging the drive system, they\n"
"would have no choice but to delay their plans...\n"
msgstr ""
"我以为破坏驱动系统，\n"
"他们就只能推迟计划……\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/17
msgid ""
"I waited until midnight and then snuck into the\n"
"hangar.\n"
msgstr ""
"我等到午夜，\n"
"悄悄溜进机库。\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/18
msgid ""
"There would be trouble if it looked like sabotage.\n"
msgstr ""
"要是被看出是破坏就麻烦了。\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/19
msgid ""
"I selected one of the drive system's load-bearing\n"
"parts and carefully worked to warp its shape.\n"
msgstr ""
"我挑了驱动系统的一处承重部件，\n"
"小心地让它变形。\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/20
msgid ""
"The legs' drive system requires a high degree of\n"
"precision to operate.\n"
msgstr ""
"腿部的驱动系统\n"
"需要极高精度的配合。\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/21
msgid ""
"Even the smallest deviation would have done it.\n"
msgstr ""
"哪怕极其微小的偏差也足够了。\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/22
msgid ""
"Then Chico walked in.\n"
msgstr ""
"这时奇科走了进来。\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/23
msgid ""
"Maybe it was one of those nights where he could\n"
"not sleep.\n"
msgstr ""
"也许是那种\n"
"睡不着觉的夜晚。\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/24
msgid ""
"In any case, he saw me, panicked, and took off\n"
"running.\n"
msgstr ""
"总之他看到我，慌了神，\n"
"转身就跑。\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/25
msgid ""
"It would have been easy to kill him. But I could not!\n"
msgstr ""
"杀他易如反掌。可我下不了手！\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/26
msgid ""
"I know he... likes me.\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道他……喜欢我。\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/27
msgid ""
"It is not as if I would ever have an interest in a\n"
"child like him...\n"
msgstr ""
"我当然不可能\n"
"对他这种小孩有兴趣……\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/28
msgid ""
"But I could not pull the trigger. Not at him. Not in\n"
"the back.\n"
msgstr ""
"可我扣不下扳机。不能对他，\n"
"更不能在背后。\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/29
msgid ""
"Will he tell them?\n"
msgstr ""
"他会说出去吗？\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/30
msgid ""
"Or is there a chance he will keep it secret?\n"
"Protect me...\n"
msgstr ""
"还是有可能替我保密？\n"
"保护我……\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/31
msgid ""
"...No.\n"
msgstr ""
"……不会。\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/32
msgid ""
"He knows now... Knows I am not who he thought I\n"
"was...\n"
msgstr ""
"他已经知道了……\n"
"知道我不是他以为的那个人……\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/33
msgid ""
"He ran without even questioning what I was doing.\n"
"There is no chance he does not know.\n"
msgstr ""
"他连问都没问就跑了，\n"
"不可能不知道。\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/34
msgid ""
"And soon, all I have built here will end.\n"
msgstr ""
"很快，我在这里建立的一切都将终结。\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/35
msgid ""
"And if Cipher has another agent among them...\n"
msgstr ""
"如果Cipher在他们之中还安插了人……\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/36
msgid ""
"If he finds out I tried to sabotage ZEKE...\n"
msgstr ""
"要是他发现我试图破坏ZEKE……\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/37
msgid ""
"This place will no longer be my \"heaven.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"这里就不再是我的「天堂」了。\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/38
msgid ""
"...Then it is settled.\n"
msgstr ""
"……那就这么定了。\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/39
msgid ""
"I make my move now.\n"
msgstr ""
"我现在就动手。\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/40
msgid ""
"Chico walked in before my sabotage was complete,\n"
"so ZEKE should still be operational.\n"
msgstr ""
"奇科进来时我的破坏还没完成，\n"
"所以ZEKE应该还能运转。\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/41
msgid ""
"It might not run at full speed or power, but I do\n"
"not have time to fix that.\n"
msgstr ""
"速度或功率也许不足，\n"
"但我没时间补救了。\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/42
msgid ""
"Without ZEKE, I do not have a chance in hell of\n"
"winning.\n"
msgstr ""
"没有ZEKE，\n"
"我根本没有胜算。\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/43
msgid ""
"I must act fast before Chico sounds the alarm...\n"
msgstr ""
"得赶在奇科报信前动手……\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/44
msgid ""
"I knew it would come to this.\n"
msgstr ""
"我就知道会有这一天。\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/45
msgid ""
"I just... did not think it would be so soon...\n"
msgstr ""
"只是……没想到会这么快……\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/46
msgid ""
"...It is time, ZEKE.\n"
msgstr ""
"……时候到了，ZEKE。\n"

#: codec/1/275/0x1135b0/47
msgid ""
"Metal Gear ZEKE, activate!\n"
msgstr ""
"METAL GEAR ZEKE，启动！\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/0
msgid ""
"She told me everything.\n"
msgstr ""
"她把一切都告诉了我。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/1
msgid ""
"Why did she open her heart to me like that?\n"
msgstr ""
"她为什么对我敞开心扉？\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/2
msgid ""
"At the time, I couldn't understand it.\n"
msgstr ""
"当时我无法理解。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/3
msgid ""
"But now I think I do.\n"
msgstr ""
"现在我想我明白了。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/5
msgid ""
"she wanted you to know the truth\n"
msgstr ""
"她想让你知道真相\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/6
msgid ""
"She chose me to tell you.\n"
msgstr ""
"她选了我来告诉你。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/7
msgid ""
"That's why she saved my life.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以她才救了我的命。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/8
msgid ""
"I've lied to you so many times. But not this time.\n"
msgstr ""
"我骗过你很多次。但这次不会。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/9
msgid ""
"My orders from the government were to obtain the\n"
"Legacy...\n"
msgstr ""
"政府给我的命令\n"
"是夺取遗产……\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/10
msgid ""
"...and to eliminate everyone who knew the truth\n"
"about what happened.\n"
msgstr ""
"……并除掉所有\n"
"知道事情真相的人。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/11
msgid ""
"In other words, I'm supposed to kill you.\n"
msgstr ""
"换句话说，我该杀了你。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/12
msgid ""
"But I can't do it.\n"
msgstr ""
"可我做不到。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/13
msgid ""
"Not because we loved each other.\n"
msgstr ""
"不是因为我们相爱过。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/14
msgid ""
"And not because you saved my life.\n"
msgstr ""
"也不是因为你救过我。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/15
msgid ""
"But because I made a promise to The Boss...\n"
msgstr ""
"而是因为我对The Boss许下过承诺……\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/16
msgid ""
"And I intend to keep it.\n"
msgstr ""
"我打算信守它。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/17
msgid ""
"I just wanted you to know.\n"
msgstr ""
"我只是想让你知道。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/18
msgid ""
"And...\n"
msgstr ""
"还有……\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/19
msgid ""
"you have to live.\n"
msgstr ""
"你必须活下去。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/20
msgid ""
"Snake, listen to me.\n"
msgstr ""
"Snake，听我说。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/21
msgid ""
"She didn't betray the United States.\n"
msgstr ""
"她没有背叛美国。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/22
msgid ""
"No, far from it. She was a hero who died for her\n"
"country.\n"
msgstr ""
"恰恰相反。\n"
"她是为国捐躯的英雄。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/23
msgid ""
"She carried out her mission knowing full well what\n"
"was going to happen.\n"
msgstr ""
"她明知结局，\n"
"依然执行了任务。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/24
msgid ""
"Self-sacrifice... because that was her duty.\n"
msgstr ""
"自我牺牲……因为那是她的职责。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/25
msgid ""
"The Boss' defection was a ruse set up by the U.S.\n"
"government.\n"
msgstr ""
"The Boss的叛逃\n"
"是美国政府设下的骗局。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/26
msgid ""
"It was all a big drama staged by Washington\n"
msgstr ""
"整件事都是华盛顿导演的一出大戏，\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/27
msgid ""
"so they could get their hands on the Philosophers'\n"
"Legacy.\n"
msgstr ""
"为的是拿到\n"
"哲学家们的遗产。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/28
msgid ""
"And The Boss was the star of the show.\n"
msgstr ""
"而The Boss是这出戏的主角。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/29
msgid ""
"They planned it so that they could get the Legacy\n"
"that Colonel Volgin inherited...\n"
msgstr ""
"他们如此谋划，是为了夺取\n"
"沃尔金上校继承的遗产……\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/30
msgid ""
"...and destroy the Shagohod at the same time.\n"
msgstr ""
"……同时摧毁Shagohod。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/31
msgid ""
"Only a legendary hero like The Boss could have\n"
"earned Volgin's trust.\n"
msgstr ""
"只有The Boss这样的传奇英雄，\n"
"才能取得沃尔金的信任。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/32
msgid ""
"Finding out where the Philosophers' Legacy was\n"
"hidden was to be her greatest mission.\n"
msgstr ""
"查出遗产的藏匿之处，\n"
"是她最重要的使命。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/33
msgid ""
"Everything was going according to plan...\n"
msgstr ""
"一切都按计划进行……\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/34
msgid ""
"But then something happened that no one could\n"
"have predicted.\n"
msgstr ""
"可接着发生了\n"
"谁也没料到的事。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/35
msgid ""
"Colonel Volgin fired an American-made nuclear\n"
"warhead at Sokolov's research facility.\n"
msgstr ""
"沃尔金上校向索科洛夫的研究所\n"
"发射了美国制造的核弹头。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/36
msgid ""
"Khrushchev demanded that the U.S. government\n"
"provide proof that it wasn't involved...\n"
msgstr ""
"赫鲁晓夫要求美国政府\n"
"拿出与此事无关的证明……\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/37
msgid ""
"They couldn't just abort the operation to steal the\n"
"Legacy.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们又不能\n"
"就此中止夺取遗产的行动。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/38
msgid ""
"So the operation itself was greatly expanded and\n"
"revised.\n"
msgstr ""
"于是行动规模\n"
"被大幅扩大和修改。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/39
msgid ""
"The authorities in Washington knew that in order\n"
"to prove its innocence,\n"
msgstr ""
"华盛顿当局清楚，\n"
"要想证明自己的清白，\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/40
msgid ""
"it had to get rid of The Boss...\n"
msgstr ""
"就必须除掉The Boss……\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/41
msgid ""
"...and that one of their own would have to do the\n"
"job.\n"
msgstr ""
"……而且必须由\n"
"他们自己的人动手。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/42
msgid ""
"The public couldn't be allowed to find out about it...\n"
"not ever.\n"
msgstr ""
"绝不能让公众知道真相……\n"
"永远不能。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/43
msgid ""
"This, they concluded, would be the best way to\n"
"keep the whole thing under wraps.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们认定，\n"
"这是把整件事捂住的最好办法。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/44
msgid ""
"The Boss wouldn't be allowed to come back home\n"
"alive.\n"
msgstr ""
"上层不许The Boss\n"
"活着回国。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/45
msgid ""
"And she wouldn't be allowed to kill herself.\n"
msgstr ""
"也不许她自尽。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/46
msgid ""
"Her life would be ended by her most beloved\n"
"disciple...\n"
msgstr ""
"她的生命将终结于\n"
"最心爱的弟子之手……\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/47
msgid ""
"That was the way the government wanted it.\n"
msgstr ""
"那是政府希望看到的结局。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/48
msgid ""
"That was the mission she was given.\n"
msgstr ""
"那是交给她的任务。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/49
msgid ""
"And she had no choice but to carry it out...\n"
msgstr ""
"而她别无选择，只能执行……\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/50
msgid ""
"Her death at your hands...\n"
msgstr ""
"她死在你手中……\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/51
msgid ""
"...was a duty she had to fulfill.\n"
msgstr ""
"……是她必须完成的职责。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/52
msgid ""
"Out of duty, she turned her back on her own\n"
"comrades...\n"
msgstr ""
"为了职责，她背弃了\n"
"自己的战友……\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/53
msgid ""
"A lesser woman would have been crushed by such\n"
"a burden...\n"
msgstr ""
"换个平庸的女人，早被\n"
"这样的重担压垮……\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/54
msgid ""
"The taint of disgrace will follow her to her grave.\n"
msgstr ""
"耻辱的污名将伴随她入土。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/55
msgid ""
"Future generations will revile her...\n"
msgstr ""
"后世会唾骂她……\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/56
msgid ""
"In America, as a despicable traitor with no sense\n"
"of honor...\n"
msgstr ""
"在美国，她是毫无廉耻\n"
"的叛徒……\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/57
msgid ""
"And in Russia, as a monster who unleashed a\n"
"nuclear catastrophe...\n"
msgstr ""
"在俄国，她是引发核灾难\n"
"的怪物……\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/58
msgid ""
"She will go down in official history as a war criminal.\n"
msgstr ""
"官方史书会记下她的战犯之名。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/59
msgid ""
"And no one will ever understand her...\n"
msgstr ""
"而永远不会有人理解她……\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/60
msgid ""
"That was her final mission.\n"
msgstr ""
"那就是她最后的任务。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/61
msgid ""
"And, like a true soldier, she saw it through to the\n"
"end.\n"
msgstr ""
"而她像一个真正的军人，\n"
"把它执行到了最后。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/62
msgid ""
"But I think she wanted you, of all people, to know\n"
"the truth.\n"
msgstr ""
"但我想，她最想让你\n"
"知道真相。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/63
msgid ""
"She wanted to live on in your memory.\n"
msgstr ""
"她想活在你的记忆里。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/64
msgid ""
"Not as a solider,\n"
msgstr ""
"不是作为一名军人，\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/65
msgid ""
"but as a woman.\n"
msgstr ""
"而是作为一个女人。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/66
msgid ""
"But she was forbidden to tell you herself.\n"
msgstr ""
"但她被禁止亲口告诉你。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/67
msgid ""
"And that's why she told me...\n"
msgstr ""
"所以她才告诉了我……\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/68
msgid ""
"Snake, history will never know what she did.\n"
msgstr ""
"斯内克，历史的书页上不会留下她的所作所为。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/69
msgid ""
"No one will ever learn the truth.\n"
msgstr ""
"永远不会有人知道真相。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/70
msgid ""
"Her story... her debriefing...\n"
msgstr ""
"她的故事……她的自白……\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/71
msgid ""
"...will endure only in your heart.\n"
msgstr ""
"……只会留在你的心里。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/72
msgid ""
"Everything she did, she did for her country.\n"
msgstr ""
"她所做的一切都是为了祖国。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/73
msgid ""
"She sacrificed her life and her honor for her native\n"
"land.\n"
msgstr ""
"她为祖国献出了\n"
"生命与荣誉。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/74
msgid ""
"She was a real hero.\n"
msgstr ""
"她是真正的英雄。\n"

#: codec/1/276/0x1145f0/75
msgid ""
"She was a true patriot.\n"
msgstr ""
"她是真正的爱国者。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/0
msgid ""
"Hello, Snake. It's been a while, hasn't it?\n"
msgstr ""
"你好啊Snake，好久不见。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/1
msgid ""
"...I hear you've been causing quite the ruckus in\n"
"Nicaragua.\n"
msgstr ""
"……听说你在尼加拉瓜\n"
"闹得挺大。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/2
msgid ""
"Nothing much to report from my end.\n"
msgstr ""
"我这边没什么可报的。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/3
msgid ""
"The Legacy's being \"put to good use\" - or so they\n"
"tell me...\n"
msgstr ""
"遗产正被「善加利用」——\n"
"他们是这样告诉我的……\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/4
msgid ""
"But enough with the small talk... there's something I\n"
"need to tell you.\n"
msgstr ""
"闲话到此为止……\n"
"有件事我必须告诉你。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/5
msgid ""
"You saw the photo that came with this tape, right?\n"
msgstr ""
"这盘磁带附带的那张照片，你看了吧？\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/6
msgid ""
"The Boss gave that to me ten years ago.\n"
msgstr ""
"那是THE BOSS十年前给我的。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/7
msgid ""
"I'm sorry. I should have told you sooner. I probably\n"
"should have told you right away.\n"
msgstr ""
"对不起。我该早点告诉你。\n"
"也许一开始就该说。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/8
msgid ""
"But sending it to you hasn't been an easy decision\n"
"to make. It's taken me ten years.\n"
msgstr ""
"但把它寄给你并不容易。\n"
"我花了十年才下定决心。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/9
msgid ""
"Once you've heard what I have to say, you'll\n"
"understand why.\n"
msgstr ""
"听完我这些话，你就会明白\n"
"为什么。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/10
msgid ""
"That photo... belonged to her.\n"
msgstr ""
"那张照片……是她的。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/11
msgid ""
"I know what you're thinking: what does she have to\n"
"do with this?\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道你在想：这和她\n"
"有什么关系？\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/12
msgid ""
"You've probably seen it a hundred times in the\n"
"press already.\n"
msgstr ""
"你大概已经在媒体上\n"
"见过它无数次了。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/13
msgid ""
"Obviously it's of the Mercury Seven, the first group\n"
"of American astronauts\n"
msgstr ""
"显然，那是水星七杰——\n"
"美国第一批宇航员。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/14
msgid ""
"- the heroes of Project Mercury.\n"
msgstr ""
"——水星计划的英雄们。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/15
msgid ""
"But there were actually eight people in that photo.\n"
msgstr ""
"但那张照片上其实有八个人。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/16
msgid ""
"One of them was edited out - erased without a\n"
"trace.\n"
msgstr ""
"其中一个被修掉了——\n"
"抹得干干净净。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/17
msgid ""
"That eighth astronaut, the one airbrushed out of\n"
"existence... that was her, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""
"那第八名宇航员，被从世上\n"
"抹去的那个……就是她，斯内克。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/18
msgid ""
"Now why did they need to keep her existence a\n"
"secret?\n"
msgstr ""
"那为什么非要隐瞒\n"
"她的存在？\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/19
msgid ""
"What were they trying to hide?\n"
msgstr ""
"他们想掩盖什么？\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/20
msgid ""
"The answer goes back even further - 17 years ago.\n"
msgstr ""
"答案还要往前推——17年前。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/21
msgid ""
"It was the height of the Cold War. The Eastern and\n"
"Western blocs were racing\n"
msgstr ""
"那是冷战最紧张的时期。\n"
"东西方阵营正在竞赛，\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/22
msgid ""
"to develop space technology to match their\n"
"nuclear arsenals.\n"
msgstr ""
"竞相发展航天技术，\n"
"以匹配各自的核武库。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/23
msgid ""
"In 1957, the Soviet Union launched Sputnik 1, the\n"
"first artificial satellite.\n"
msgstr ""
"1957年，苏联发射了\n"
"第一颗人造卫星斯普特尼克1号。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/24
msgid ""
"The Americans were stunned.\n"
msgstr ""
"美国人大为震惊。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/25
msgid ""
"They'd been led to believe their country led the\n"
"world in science and technology.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们一直以为自己的国家\n"
"在科技上领先世界。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/26
msgid ""
"That shock quickly turned into fear.\n"
msgstr ""
"震惊很快变成了恐惧。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/27
msgid ""
"If the Russians had the know-how to launch a\n"
"satellite into space,\n"
msgstr ""
"既然俄国人有本事把卫星\n"
"送上太空，\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/28
msgid ""
"they could use it to launch a nuclear missile, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"也就能用它发射核导弹。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/29
msgid ""
"Frantic, the U.S. threw everything it had into the\n"
"space race.\n"
msgstr ""
"美国慌了手脚，把一切\n"
"都投入太空竞赛。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/30
msgid ""
"The following year, the Army succeeded in\n"
"launching the first American satellite, Explorer 1.\n"
msgstr ""
"第二年，陆军成功发射了\n"
"美国第一颗卫星探险者1号。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/31
msgid ""
"The National Aeronautics and Space Administration\n"
"was established that fall,\n"
msgstr ""
"那年秋天，NASA\n"
"正式成立，\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/32
msgid ""
"and Project Mercury with it.\n"
msgstr ""
"水星计划也应运而生。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/33
msgid ""
"The goal was to send a man into space... and\n"
"seven men were chosen as pilot candidates.\n"
msgstr ""
"目标是把人送上太空……\n"
"于是七人被选为飞行员候选人。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/34
msgid ""
"The media dubbed them the Mercury Seven.\n"
msgstr ""
"媒体称他们为水星七杰。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/35
msgid ""
"They were immediately hailed as national heroes,\n"
"icons of Western space exploration.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们立刻被奉为民族英雄，\n"
"西方航天探索的象征。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/36
msgid ""
"But after Explorer, America suffered a series of\n"
"failed rocket launches.\n"
msgstr ""
"但在探险者之后，美国\n"
"的火箭发射接连失败。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/37
msgid ""
"Desperate, the government made a fateful decision.\n"
msgstr ""
"政府孤注一掷，做出了决定命运的选择。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/38
msgid ""
"Unable to wait for its space program to mature,\n"
"they'd steal the Soviets' technology,\n"
msgstr ""
"他们等不及航天计划成熟，\n"
"决定去偷苏联的技术，\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/39
msgid ""
"at the same time sabotaging their space program.\n"
msgstr ""
"同时破坏他们的航天计划。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/40
msgid ""
"You know better than anyone how hard a mission\n"
"that was.\n"
msgstr ""
"那任务有多艰巨，\n"
"你比谁都清楚。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/41
msgid ""
"The Soviet space program was shrouded in secrecy.\n"
msgstr ""
"苏联的航天计划高度保密。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/42
msgid ""
"Recovering that information would be no easy task.\n"
msgstr ""
"要拿到那些情报绝非易事。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/43
msgid ""
"Using the help of an insider, they'd insert a sleeper\n"
"agent into the research institute,\n"
msgstr ""
"借助内应，他们会往研究所\n"
"安插一名潜伏特工，\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/44
msgid ""
"or else recruit one of those insiders to do the job\n"
"for them...\n"
msgstr ""
"或者干脆策反一名\n"
"内部人员替他们办事……\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/45
msgid ""
"And, if necessary, the mission leader would have to\n"
"go in and sort things out themselves.\n"
msgstr ""
"必要时，任务指挥官\n"
"还得亲自潜入收拾局面。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/46
msgid ""
"Someone was needed with experience, knowledge,\n"
"and superior intuition...\n"
msgstr ""
"这需要经验、知识\n"
"与过人直觉的人……\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/47
msgid ""
"And the only one for the job was The Boss.\n"
msgstr ""
"而唯一胜任的只有THE BOSS。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/48
msgid ""
"The President himself asked for her by name.\n"
msgstr ""
"总统亲自点名要她。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/49
msgid ""
"He needed someone who could be trusted with the\n"
"fate of a nation.\n"
msgstr ""
"他需要一个能把国家命运\n"
"托付出去的人。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/50
msgid ""
"Who else to turn to but the hero of the Second\n"
"World War?\n"
msgstr ""
"除了二战的英雄，\n"
"还能找谁？\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/51
msgid ""
"It was June 1959.\n"
msgstr ""
"那是1959年6月。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/52
msgid ""
"So you see, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""
"你明白了吧，斯内克。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/53
msgid ""
"That's why she left. That was the top-secret\n"
"mission that took her from you.\n"
msgstr ""
"她就是这样离开的。那项\n"
"绝密任务把她从你身边带走。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/54
msgid ""
"But her selection ruffled a few CIA feathers.\n"
msgstr ""
"但她的入选让中情局有些不快。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/55
msgid ""
"They didn't appreciate the President going over\n"
"their head like that.\n"
msgstr ""
"总统这样越过他们，\n"
"让他们很不痛快。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/56
msgid ""
"The mission was tough enough already, and now\n"
"the CIA was dragging its feet.\n"
msgstr ""
"任务本已够艰难，\n"
"中情局还拖后腿。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/57
msgid ""
"She couldn't get anything out of them - no\n"
"manpower, no information.\n"
msgstr ""
"她从他们那里什么都\n"
"要不到——没人手，没情报。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/58
msgid ""
"Left to her own devices,\n"
msgstr ""
"无奈之下，\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/59
msgid ""
"The Boss made a decision she knew would come\n"
"back to haunt her.\n"
msgstr ""
"THE BOSS做出了一个她知道\n"
"会反噬自身的决定。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/60
msgid ""
"She decided to tap into the Philosophers' network.\n"
msgstr ""
"她决定动用哲学家们的网络。\n"

#: codec/1/277/0x115da0/61
msgid ""
"And that's when the wheels of fate began to turn.\n"
msgstr ""
"命运的齿轮就此开始转动。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/0
msgid ""
"The Philosophers were a secret society of\n"
"powerbrokers formed in a pact\n"
msgstr ""
"哲学家们是一个由权贵组成的秘密结社，\n"
"源自20世纪初的一纸盟约\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/1
msgid ""
"between the U.S., Russia, and China in the early\n"
"20th century.\n"
msgstr ""
"由美国、俄国和中国\n"
"在20世纪初订立。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/2
msgid ""
"Of course, by that time the American and Soviet\n"
"branches had already parted ways.\n"
msgstr ""
"当然，那时美国和苏联的分支\n"
"早已分道扬镳。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/3
msgid ""
"But there were those among the remaining Russian\n"
"Philosophers\n"
msgstr ""
"但留在俄国的哲学家之中，\n"
"仍有人\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/4
msgid ""
"not entirely happy with the one-party Communist\n"
"state.\n"
msgstr ""
"对一党专政的共产主义体制\n"
"并不满意。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/5
msgid ""
"The Boss reached out to them.\n"
msgstr ""
"The Boss主动接触了他们。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/6
msgid ""
"She arranged clandestine meetings in Berlin, hoping\n"
"to find a way into OKB-1,\n"
msgstr ""
"她在柏林安排秘密会面，\n"
"希望打进OKB-1，\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/7
msgid ""
"the Soviets' premier design bureau.\n"
msgstr ""
"苏联首屈一指的设计局。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/8
msgid ""
"She worked tirelessly to win their sympathy - in\n"
"some instances using huge sums of cash,\n"
msgstr ""
"她不遗余力地博取他们的同情——\n"
"有时用巨额现金，\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/9
msgid ""
"in others by helping them over the Berlin Wall.\n"
msgstr ""
"有时帮他们翻越柏林墙。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/10
msgid ""
"It was a dangerous game to be playing.\n"
msgstr ""
"这是一场危险的游戏。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/11
msgid ""
"The Philosophers had everything on her. And not\n"
"just information, either.\n"
msgstr ""
"哲学家们掌握着她的一切。\n"
"而且不只是情报。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/12
msgid ""
"She'd given birth to a child on the battlefield, only\n"
"to have them immediately snatch it away.\n"
msgstr ""
"她曾在战场上生下孩子，\n"
"却立刻被他们夺走。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/13
msgid ""
"I know she told you that story.\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道她跟你说过这件事。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/14
msgid ""
"If that child was in the hands of the Soviet\n"
"Philosophers,\n"
msgstr ""
"如果那个孩子\n"
"落在苏联哲学家手里，\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/15
msgid ""
"she'd be putting more than just herself in danger.\n"
msgstr ""
"她危及的就不止自己了。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/16
msgid ""
"But she did what she had to do.\n"
msgstr ""
"但她做了该做的事。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/17
msgid ""
"At the time, the Soviet Union was believed to have\n"
"an arsenal of missiles\n"
msgstr ""
"当时人们相信苏联\n"
"拥有大量导弹，\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/18
msgid ""
"far greater than that of the United States.\n"
msgstr ""
"远多于美国。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/19
msgid ""
"If that proved to be the case, Moscow would be\n"
"free from the yoke of nuclear deterrence...\n"
msgstr ""
"若真是这样，莫斯科就能\n"
"摆脱核威慑的枷锁……\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/20
msgid ""
"Raising the possibility that the Soviets might\n"
"actually launch nukes\n"
msgstr ""
"这样一来，苏联\n"
"就有可能真的动用核武器\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/21
msgid ""
"- if they felt it necessary.\n"
msgstr ""
"——只要他们认为有必要。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/22
msgid ""
"As you know, the so-called missile gap turned out\n"
"to be a Soviet bluff.\n"
msgstr ""
"如你所知，所谓导弹差距\n"
"其实是苏联的虚张声势。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/23
msgid ""
"Moscow'd gone to incredible lengths to perpetuate\n"
"the lie.\n"
msgstr ""
"莫斯科为了维持这个谎言\n"
"费尽心机。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/24
msgid ""
"In fact, the whole space race was really just a part\n"
"of an elaborate ruse.\n"
msgstr ""
"事实上，整个太空竞赛\n"
"也是这场骗局的一环。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/25
msgid ""
"Only we didn't know that at the time.\n"
msgstr ""
"只是当时我们并不知道。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/26
msgid ""
"She used to joke that even she swallowed the\n"
"whole missile gap story hook, line, and sinker.\n"
msgstr ""
"她常开玩笑说，连自己都\n"
"对导弹差距的说法深信不疑。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/27
msgid ""
"She put her life on the line for the sake of her\n"
"country - to prevent nuclear war.\n"
msgstr ""
"她为祖国赌上性命，\n"
"只为阻止核战争。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/28
msgid ""
"And it was because of her sacrificial efforts that\n"
"America succeeded\n"
msgstr ""
"正是靠她牺牲般的努力，\n"
"美国才成功\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/29
msgid ""
"in placing a sleeper agent inside OKB-1.\n"
msgstr ""
"把一名潜伏特工安插进OKB-1。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/30
msgid ""
"NASA began to receive huge volumes of technical\n"
"data from the Soviet program.\n"
msgstr ""
"NASA开始收到大量\n"
"来自苏联计划的技术资料。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/31
msgid ""
"By the end of 1959,\n"
msgstr ""
"到1959年底，\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/32
msgid ""
"they'd succeeded in sending a chimpanzee named\n"
"Sam on a ballistic rocket flight.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们成功让一只叫山姆的黑猩猩\n"
"乘弹道火箭飞了一趟。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/33
msgid ""
"The rocket never left the atmosphere,\n"
msgstr ""
"火箭没有飞出大气层，\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/34
msgid ""
"but all the same it was a huge success for NASA,\n"
msgstr ""
"但对NASA来说仍是巨大成功，\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/35
msgid ""
"restoring confidence in its technology.\n"
msgstr ""
"重新树立了对技术的信心。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/36
msgid ""
"Then, just when the operation was starting to\n"
"produce results, the CIA came calling.\n"
msgstr ""
"就在行动初见成果时，\n"
"中情局找上门来。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/37
msgid ""
"\"You're a war hero,\" they said.\n"
msgstr ""
"「你是战争英雄，」他们说。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/38
msgid ""
"\"No need for you to dirty your hands with this sort\n"
"of black ops.\n"
msgstr ""
"「不必为这种黑色行动\n"
"弄脏你的手。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/39
msgid ""
"We'll take it from here.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"接下来交给我们。」\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/40
msgid ""
"In effect, they wanted to reap the rewards for\n"
"themselves.\n"
msgstr ""
"说白了，\n"
"他们想独占果实。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/41
msgid ""
"But The Boss didn't object. \"My part is over,\" she\n"
"said.\n"
msgstr ""
"但The Boss没有反对。\n"
"「我的戏份结束了，」她说。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/42
msgid ""
"\"I don't care what you do with the data now.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"「那些资料你们怎么处理都行。」\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/43
msgid ""
"It seemed as if NASA was making great strides\n"
"toward manned spaceflight\n"
msgstr ""
"NASA似乎正大步迈向\n"
"载人航天，\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/44
msgid ""
"while the Russians lagged behind.\n"
msgstr ""
"而俄国人落在后面。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/45
msgid ""
"They even got a report from their mole at OKB-1.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们甚至收到了安插在OKB-1的内线的报告。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/46
msgid ""
"\"The safe return of Sam has sent our scientists\n"
"into a panic,\" he said.\n"
msgstr ""
"“萨姆平安归来，让我们的\n"
"科学家陷入恐慌，”他说。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/47
msgid ""
"Soon afterward, the Soviet Union sent an animal of\n"
"its own into space on Sputnik 2,\n"
msgstr ""
"不久之后，苏联用斯普特尼克2号\n"
"把自己的动物送上了太空，\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/48
msgid ""
"the dog Kudryavka - better known to the world as\n"
"Laika.\n"
msgstr ""
"那只狗叫库德里亚夫卡——\n"
"世人更熟悉的名字是莱卡。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/49
msgid ""
"But Laika was fated never to return to Earth.\n"
msgstr ""
"但莱卡注定再也回不了地球。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/50
msgid ""
"The U.S. can recover its spacecraft from the\n"
"ocean upon reentry.\n"
msgstr ""
"美国能在航天器返回时\n"
"从海上回收。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/51
msgid ""
"But the Soviet Union only borders the frozen Arctic.\n"
msgstr ""
"但苏联只濒临冰封的北冰洋。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/52
msgid ""
"They had to bring their spacecraft down on land.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们只能让航天器在陆地着陆。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/53
msgid ""
"How could they soften the impact enough to bring\n"
"a living creature back safely?\n"
msgstr ""
"要怎样缓冲着陆的冲击，\n"
"才能让活物安全返回？\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/54
msgid ""
"The agent reported that the Soviets hadn't yet\n"
"found a solution to that problem.\n"
msgstr ""
"特工报告说，苏联还没\n"
"解决这个问题。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/55
msgid ""
"The plot to sabotage the Soviet space program\n"
"seemed to be working, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"破坏苏联航天计划的行动\n"
"似乎也在奏效。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/56
msgid ""
"First they tampered with Sputnik 4's reentry.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们先是在斯普特尼克4号的返回上动了手脚。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/57
msgid ""
"Then, two months later, one of their rockets\n"
"exploded on the launch pad.\n"
msgstr ""
"两个月后，他们的一枚火箭\n"
"在发射台上爆炸。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/58
msgid ""
"They did manage to send two dogs into orbit\n"
"aboard Sputnik 5\n"
msgstr ""
"他们确实用斯普特尼克5号\n"
"把两只狗送上了轨道，\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/59
msgid ""
"- and return them safely to Earth - but the agent\n"
"dismissed it as a fluke.\n"
msgstr ""
"——并安全带回地球——\n"
"但特工认为那只是侥幸。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/60
msgid ""
"Dogs, sure, but humans? They didn't have the\n"
"technology.\n"
msgstr ""
"狗可以，人可不行。\n"
"他们没那技术。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/61
msgid ""
"Everybody believed it. Everybody was complacent.\n"
msgstr ""
"所有人都信了，都松懈了。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/62
msgid ""
"Everybody... except The Boss.\n"
msgstr ""
"所有人……除了THE BOSS。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/63
msgid ""
"There was something about the Sputnik 5\n"
"schematics\n"
msgstr ""
"斯普特尼克5号的设计图里\n"
"有处不对劲，\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/64
msgid ""
"they were getting that didn't seem right.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们拿到的那些图纸，总有些蹊跷。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/65
msgid ""
"Some kind of ejection device on the capsule that\n"
"didn't quite belong.\n"
msgstr ""
"返回舱上有个不该\n"
"出现的弹射装置。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/66
msgid ""
"She couldn't figure out the reason why it was\n"
"there. What was it supposed to eject?\n"
msgstr ""
"她想不明白它为什么在那。\n"
"它到底要弹射什么？\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/67
msgid ""
"NASA shrugged off her concerns.\n"
msgstr ""
"NASA对她的担忧不以为意。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/68
msgid ""
"They figured it was probably meant to eject the\n"
"flight recorder in case of an accident.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们觉得那大概是出事故时\n"
"用来弹射飞行记录仪的。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/69
msgid ""
"The Boss pleaded with them to investigate, but the\n"
"CIA wasn't having it.\n"
msgstr ""
"THE BOSS恳求他们调查，\n"
"中情局却不买账。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/70
msgid ""
"They probably thought she was trying to reclaim\n"
"some of the glory for herself.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们大概以为她想为自己\n"
"抢回一些功名。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/71
msgid ""
"The Boss wouldn't give up. She decided to head to\n"
"the Soviet Union herself.\n"
msgstr ""
"THE BOSS不肯放弃。\n"
"她决定亲自前往苏联。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/72
msgid ""
"Alone. Without any backing from the CIA.\n"
msgstr ""
"独自一人。没有中情局的任何支援。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/73
msgid ""
"By the beginning of the next year - 1961 - she'd\n"
"succeeded in infiltrating OKB-1.\n"
msgstr ""
"到第二年年初——1961年——\n"
"她成功潜入了OKB-1。\n"

#: codec/1/279/0x117460/74
msgid ""
"That's when she saw the truth for the first time.\n"
msgstr ""
"就在那时，她第一次看见了真相。\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/0
msgid ""
"The sleeper that she'd worked so hard to place\n"
"was a double agent.\n"
msgstr ""
"她费尽心思安插的卧底\n"
"是个双面间谍。\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/1
msgid ""
"He'd been turned by the Soviets and was feeding\n"
"the Americans lies.\n"
msgstr ""
"他被苏联人策反，一直在给\n"
"美国人喂假情报。\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/2
msgid ""
"But what shocked The Boss even more was why.\n"
msgstr ""
"但更让THE BOSS震惊的是原因。\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/3
msgid ""
"The CIA's access agent had been taking a large\n"
"cut of the sleeper's pay.\n"
msgstr ""
"CIA特工一直从这潜伏者薪水里\n"
"抽走一大笔。\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/4
msgid ""
"The sleeper felt what little he was left with wasn't\n"
"worth the risk.\n"
msgstr ""
"潜伏者觉得剩下的这点钱\n"
"不值得冒这个险。\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/5
msgid ""
"When he got a better offer from Moscow, he took\n"
"it.\n"
msgstr ""
"莫斯科给更好条件，他就接了\n"
"。\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/6
msgid ""
"At some point,\n"
msgstr ""
"不知何时\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/7
msgid ""
"the Americans' intelligence operation had become\n"
"an open book to the Soviets.\n"
msgstr ""
"美国人的情报行动对苏联人来说\n"
"已是一本摊开的书。\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/8
msgid ""
"And contrary to what the sleeper'd been reporting,\n"
msgstr ""
"而与潜伏者一直汇报的相反，\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/9
msgid ""
"the Soviets' manned spaceflight technology was\n"
"quite advanced.\n"
msgstr ""
"苏联的载人航天技术\n"
"相当先进。\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/10
msgid ""
"It wasn't until she infiltrated OKB-1 herself\n"
msgstr ""
"直到她亲自潜入OKB-1，\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/11
msgid ""
"that The Boss learned the truth about Sputnik 5.\n"
msgstr ""
"THE BOSS才得知人造卫星5号的真相。\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/12
msgid ""
"After the spacecraft reentered the atmosphere, it\n"
"ejected the pilot\n"
msgstr ""
"飞船重返大气层后，在7000米高空\n"
"弹射出飞行员\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/13
msgid ""
"- seat and all - at an altitude of 7,000 meters.\n"
msgstr ""
"- 连同座椅一起。\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/14
msgid ""
"It was the Soviets' solution to the problem of land\n"
"recovery.\n"
msgstr ""
"这是苏联人对土地\n"
"恢复问题的解决方案。\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/15
msgid ""
"The mystery device attached to Sputnik 5 was for\n"
"that purpose.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sputnik 5上的神秘装置就为\n"
"此而设。\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/16
msgid ""
"The pilot would parachute down from that high\n"
"altitude wearing a bulky spacesuit...\n"
msgstr ""
"飞行员将穿着笨重的宇航服从那样的高空\n"
"跳伞降落……\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/17
msgid ""
"Crazy, I know.\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道，很疯狂。\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/18
msgid ""
"The Soviets knew exactly how dangerous it was, of\n"
"course.\n"
msgstr ""
"当然，苏联人非常清楚它有多危险\n"
"。\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/19
msgid ""
"So much so that they gave Yuri Gagarin, the first\n"
"man in space,\n"
msgstr ""
"以至于他们给了尤里·加加林，首位\n"
"太空人，\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/20
msgid ""
"a special two-rank promotion before reentry.\n"
msgstr ""
"在重返前特批连升两级。\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/21
msgid ""
"Only Moscow could come up with this kind of plan.\n"
msgstr ""
"只有莫斯科才想得出这种计划。\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/22
msgid ""
"With total state control over information,\n"
msgstr ""
"凭借国家对信息的全面控制，\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/23
msgid ""
"they could easily pretend it never happened in the\n"
"event of a failure...\n"
msgstr ""
"一旦失败，他们可以轻易装作\n"
"从未发生……\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/24
msgid ""
"The Boss passed the info on to NASA. It was their\n"
"worst nightmare.\n"
msgstr ""
"THE BOSS把情报给了NASA。那是他们\n"
"最可怕的噩梦。\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/25
msgid ""
"The glory of mankind's first spaceflight was about\n"
"to be stolen from them by the Soviet Union.\n"
msgstr ""
"人类首次太空飞行的荣耀即将\n"
"被苏联夺走。\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/26
msgid ""
"It was Sputnik all over again...\n"
msgstr ""
"又是人造卫星重演……\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/27
msgid ""
"And the CIA was caught no less off guard.\n"
msgstr ""
"CIA也同样措手不及。\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/28
msgid ""
"Their ineptitude had caused the fiasco in the first\n"
"place.\n"
msgstr ""
"正是他们的无能\n"
"才导致了这场惨败。\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/29
msgid ""
"The Soviets' deception was brilliant. They'd woven\n"
"a masterful tapestry of truth and fiction\n"
msgstr ""
"苏联人的欺骗手段堪称绝妙。他们编织了\n"
"一幅真假交织的精妙画卷\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/30
msgid ""
"to convince the Americans their intelligence\n"
"operations were proceeding as planned.\n"
msgstr ""
"让美国人相信他们的情报\n"
"行动正按计划进行。\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/31
msgid ""
"No one but The Boss could have seen through it...\n"
msgstr ""
"除了THE BOSS，没人能看穿……\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/32
msgid ""
"It was obvious the Soviets had some gifted minds\n"
"working on their side.\n"
msgstr ""
"显然苏联人有一些\n"
"天赋异禀的人才在为他们效力。\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/33
msgid ""
"But that certainly didn't excuse the CIA's massive\n"
"failure.\n"
msgstr ""
"但这绝不能为中央情报局的重大\n"
"失误开脱。\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/34
msgid ""
"The CIA wasn't done, though,\n"
msgstr ""
"但CIA没罢手，\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/35
msgid ""
"and devised an ingenious plan to avoid taking\n"
"responsibility.\n"
msgstr ""
"并设计了一个巧妙的计划来逃避\n"
"承担责任。\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/36
msgid ""
"Luckily for them, a new President had been elected\n"
"the previous November - John F. Kennedy.\n"
msgstr ""
"对他们来说幸运的是，前一年十一月新当选了一位总统——约翰·F·肯尼迪。\n"
"\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/37
msgid ""
"As he didn't know the case history when taking\n"
"office,\n"
msgstr ""
"由于他上任时并不了解事件的来龙去脉，\n"
"\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/38
msgid ""
"the CIA was able to feed lies to his new\n"
"administration.\n"
msgstr ""
"中情局得以向他新组建的政府灌输谎言。\n"
"\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/39
msgid ""
"They masked their own failures, placing the blame\n"
"squarely on The Boss's shoulders.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们掩盖了自己的失败，把责任一股脑儿推到了“头儿”的肩上。\n"
"\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/40
msgid ""
"After all, she'd selected an unreliable sleeper.\n"
msgstr ""
"毕竟，她选了个靠不住的潜伏者。\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/41
msgid ""
"They claimed she'd failed to make use of one of\n"
"the most effective means\n"
msgstr ""
"他们声称她没能利用起最有效的手段之一，\n"
"\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/42
msgid ""
"of controlling a sleeper agent's actions.\n"
msgstr ""
"即控制其行动的办法。\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/43
msgid ""
"Holding their family hostage.\n"
msgstr ""
"扣押其家人当人质。\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/44
msgid ""
"The Boss was well aware that would have worked -\n"
"she told me so later.\n"
msgstr ""
"“头儿”很清楚那样做本会奏效——她后来告诉了我。\n"
"\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/45
msgid ""
"But she couldn't bring herself to do it...\n"
msgstr ""
"但她下不了手……\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/46
msgid ""
"It seems clear it had to do with having her own\n"
"child taken.\n"
msgstr ""
"看来很明显，这与她自己的孩子被人夺走有关。\n"
"\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/47
msgid ""
"She could never inflict the same pain on anyone\n"
"else.\n"
msgstr ""
"她绝不会把同样的痛苦加诸于任何人身上。\n"
"\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/48
msgid ""
"The CIA used that against her.\n"
msgstr ""
"CIA利用这点对付她。\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/49
msgid ""
"In his election campaign, Kennedy had vowed to\n"
"close the missile gap with Moscow.\n"
msgstr ""
"在竞选活动中，肯尼迪曾誓言要弥合与莫斯科之间的导弹差距。\n"
"\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/50
msgid ""
"If America lost the space race, that promise would\n"
"be worthless.\n"
msgstr ""
"如果美国输掉了太空竞赛，那个承诺就将一文不值。\n"
"\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/51
msgid ""
"The fact that the President had no links to the\n"
"Philosophers only made things worse.\n"
msgstr ""
"总统与“哲人”毫无关联，这反而让情况变得更糟。\n"
"\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/52
msgid ""
"He was completely unaware of the secret networks\n"
"she'd used to complete her mission.\n"
msgstr ""
"他完全不知道她曾利用哪些秘密网络来完成自己的任务。\n"
"\n"

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/53
msgid ""
"In his eyes, she was no better than a traitor.\n"
msgstr ""
"在他眼里，她无异于叛徒。\n"
